// E0203: a path whose module prefix names nothing must NOT resolve.
//
// This is the CONTROL for its sibling,
// tests/tests/negative/E0203_path_drops_trailing_segment.cryo. That case pins
// a path naming a REAL module that does not declare the item; this one pins a
// prefix naming NO module at all.
//
// The pair is what makes either meaningful. Before the 2026-08-04 fix the
// sibling COMPILED and this one did not, which is what showed the defect was
// `module_ns_matches_prefix` specifically rather than path qualifiers being
// ignored wholesale. Both green afterwards shows the matcher was tightened
// without turning path resolution into a blanket rejection.
//
// CORRECT behavior, before and after the fix. Must stay green through the
// keystone (spec §5.2) and the M1 deletion; if it goes red, path resolution
// stopped rejecting unknown prefixes rather than starting to reject wrong
// ones.
![config(testing)]
![config(negative, E0203)]
namespace CryoTests::Negative::E0203UnknownModulePrefix;
function cf_use() -> void {
    const w: NoSuchMod::Inner::Widget = NoSuchMod::Inner::Widget { v: 1 };   //~ ERROR[E0203] cannot find type `NoSuchMod::Inner::Widget` in
}
function main() -> int { return 0; }
